declare
  v_plan constant jsonb := $audit_plan${"generatedBy":"scripts/prod-open/sat-expr-only-fixes-sql.ts","problems":[{"patch_id":"E1019-X001","problem_id":"4cc47e7c-e766-47d8-aa9b-ae16aeb96d71","from_version_id":"c3016076-a78c-4498-a0c9-326fe8691b3d","expect":{"explanation":"Substitute h = 3 into C = 25h + 45: C = 25(3) + 45 = 75 + 45 = 120. So the total cost is \\$120. Choice A (70) incorrectly computes 25(3) - 5 or similar miscalculation. Choice B (75) only accounts for the hourly charge (25 × 3) and omits the flat fee of \\$45. Choice D (150) incorrectly adds the flat fee twice or uses 25(3+3).","explanation_en":"Substitute h = 3 into C = 25h + 45: C = 25(3) + 45 = 75 + 45 = 120. So the total cost is \\$120, which makes C the correct choice. Choice A (70) comes from a miscalculation such as 25(3) - 5. Choice B (75) only counts the hourly charge (25 × 3) and leaves out the flat fee of \\$45. Choice D (150) comes from adding the flat fee twice or from computing 25(3+3)."},"set":{"explanation":"Substitute h = 3 into C = 25h + 45: C = 25(3) + 45 = 75 + 45 = 120. So the total cost is \\$120. Choice A (70) comes from adding the hourly rate and the flat fee once (25 + 45) instead of multiplying the rate by 3 hours. Choice B (75) only accounts for the hourly charge (25 × 3) and omits the flat fee of \\$45. Choice D (150) comes from using 6 hours instead of 3, that is, 25(3 + 3) = 150.","explanation_en":"Substitute h = 3 into C = 25h + 45: C = 25(3) + 45 = 75 + 45 = 120. So the total cost is \\$120, which makes C the correct choice. Choice A (70) comes from adding the hourly rate and the flat fee once (25 + 45) instead of multiplying the rate by 3 hours. Choice B (75) only counts the hourly charge (25 × 3) and leaves out the flat fee of \\$45. Choice D (150) comes from using 6 hours instead of 3, that is, 25(3 + 3) = 150."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T06:01:34.918Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-X001","fromVersionId":"c3016076-a78c-4498-a0c9-326fe8691b3d","fromVersionNo":4}},{"patch_id":"E1019-X002","problem_id":"9977438d-6d27-48ed-aebb-c4ad8e08c6c0","from_version_id":"579dc6f5-3508-4388-9631-895bb1d38cbb","expect":{"explanation":"$2y - 4x = 6$을 정리하면 $y = 2x + 3$이고, $y + 2x = 13$을 정리하면 $y = -2x + 13$이다. 두 식을 연립하면 $2x + 3 = -2x + 13$이므로 $4x = 10$, $x = 2.5$이다. 이를 $y = 2x + 3$에 대입하면 $y = 2(2.5) + 3 = 5 + 3 = 8$이다. 따라서 두 직선의 교점은 $(2.5, 8)$이고, 정답은 $y = 8$이다.\n\n오답 분석:\n- 3: $y = 2x+3$에서 $x=0$일 때의 $y$절편 값으로, 교점이 아닌 절편을 답으로 착각한 경우이다.\n- 5: $2x+3=-2x+13$에서 $4x=10$을 잘못 계산해 $x=2$로 두고 $y=2(2)+3=7$이 아니라 단순 계산 실수로 5를 얻은 경우이다 (예: $x$ 대신 상수항만 고려).\n- 10: $y=-2x+13$에서 $x=1.5$ 등 잘못된 $x$값을 대입해 얻을 수 있는 오답이다.","explanation_en":"Rearranging $2y - 4x = 6$ gives $y = 2x + 3$, and rearranging $y + 2x = 13$ gives $y = -2x + 13$. Setting the two equal gives $2x + 3 = -2x + 13$, so $4x = 10$ and $x = 2.5$. Substituting into $y = 2x + 3$ gives $y = 2(2.5) + 3 = 5 + 3 = 8$. So the two lines intersect at $(2.5, 8)$, and the answer is $y = 8$.\n\nWrong-answer analysis:\n- 3: This is the $y$-intercept value of $y = 2x+3$ at $x=0$, mistaking an intercept for the intersection.\n- 5: This comes from miscalculating $4x=10$ in $2x+3=-2x+13$ and getting $x=2$, then reaching 5 through a simple arithmetic slip instead of $y=2(2)+3=7$ (for example, considering only the constant term instead of $x$).\n- 10: This is a wrong answer you can get by substituting a wrong $x$ value, such as $x=1.5$, into $y=-2x+13$."},"set":{"explanation":"$2y - 4x = 6$을 정리하면 $y = 2x + 3$이고, $y + 2x = 13$을 정리하면 $y = -2x + 13$이다. 두 식을 연립하면 $2x + 3 = -2x + 13$이므로 $4x = 10$, $x = 2.5$이다. 이를 $y = 2x + 3$에 대입하면 $y = 2(2.5) + 3 = 5 + 3 = 8$이다. 따라서 두 직선의 교점은 $(2.5, 8)$이고, 정답은 $y = 8$이다.\n\n오답 분석:\n- 3: $y = 2x+3$에서 $x=0$일 때의 $y$절편 값으로, 교점이 아닌 절편을 답으로 착각한 경우이다.\n- 5: $x = 2.5$일 때 $2x = 5$에서 멈추고 상수항 $3$을 더하지 않은 경우이다.\n- 10: $y=-2x+13$에서 $x=1.5$ 등 잘못된 $x$값을 대입해 얻을 수 있는 오답이다.","explanation_en":"Rearranging $2y - 4x = 6$ gives $y = 2x + 3$, and rearranging $y + 2x = 13$ gives $y = -2x + 13$. Setting the two equal gives $2x + 3 = -2x + 13$, so $4x = 10$ and $x = 2.5$. Substituting into $y = 2x + 3$ gives $y = 2(2.5) + 3 = 5 + 3 = 8$. So the two lines intersect at $(2.5, 8)$, and the answer is $y = 8$.\n\nWrong-answer analysis:\n- 3: This is the $y$-intercept value of $y = 2x+3$ at $x=0$, mistaking an intercept for the intersection.\n- 5: This is the value of $2x$ when $x = 2.5$; it comes from stopping before adding the constant term $3$.\n- 10: This is a wrong answer you can get by substituting a wrong $x$ value, such as $x=1.5$, into $y=-2x+13$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T06:01:34.924Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-X002","fromVersionId":"579dc6f5-3508-4388-9631-895bb1d38cbb","fromVersionNo":2}},{"patch_id":"E1019-X003","problem_id":"f59b7f57-b596-4235-9902-d8036d9040ff","from_version_id":"ea26c0bd-cb4e-4e94-a8f6-67a7c3c19c80","expect":{"passage":"A community garden sells tomato seedlings and pepper seedlings at a spring plant sale. Each tomato seedling sells for $6$ and each pepper seedling sells for $3$. The system of equations below represents two conditions on a day when $x$ tomato seedlings and $y$ pepper seedlings were sold: the total sales revenue was $120$ dollars, and the total number of seedlings sold was $30$.\n\n$6x + 3y = 120$\n$x + y = 30$"},"set":{"passage":"A community garden sells tomato seedlings and pepper seedlings at a spring plant sale. Each tomato seedling sells for \\$6 and each pepper seedling sells for \\$3. The system of equations below represents two conditions on a day when $x$ tomato seedlings and $y$ pepper seedlings were sold: the total sales revenue was $120$ dollars, and the total number of seedlings sold was $30$.\n\n$6x + 3y = 120$\n$x + y = 30$"},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T06:01:34.925Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-X003","fromVersionId":"ea26c0bd-cb4e-4e94-a8f6-67a7c3c19c80","fromVersionNo":2}},{"patch_id":"E1019-X004","problem_id":"7ddfae40-f506-48b2-a2c2-fd8dab606f30","from_version_id":"8ec1cc49-c5e4-48bb-b9a6-7a164aedf241","expect":{"passage":"A museum curator is planning an exhibit space and wants to display paintings and sculptures together. Each painting requires 8 square feet of wall space, and each sculpture requires 15 square feet of floor space. The exhibit has at most 240 square feet of combined space available for these two types of art. The curator also wants to display at least 5 paintings. Let $x$ represent the number of paintings and $y$ represent the number of sculptures. The graph shows the boundary lines $x = 5$ and $8x + 15y = 240$.","figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":30,"min":0,"step":5,"title":"Number of paintings (x)"},"y":{"max":25,"min":0,"step":5,"title":"Number of sculptures (y)"}},"objects":[{"id":"l1","intercept":16,"kind":"line","label":"8x + 15y = 240","slope":-0.5333},{"id":"l2","kind":"line","label":"x = 5","through":[[5,0],[5,25]]}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"passage":"A museum curator is planning an exhibit space and wants to display paintings and sculptures together. Each painting requires 8 square feet of space, and each sculpture requires 15 square feet of space. The exhibit has at most 240 square feet of combined space available for these two types of art. The curator also wants to display at least 5 paintings. Let $x$ represent the number of paintings and $y$ represent the number of sculptures.","figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T06:01:34.927Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-X004","fromVersionId":"8ec1cc49-c5e4-48bb-b9a6-7a164aedf241","fromVersionNo":3}}],"sets":[]}$audit_plan$::jsonb;
  v_actor uuid := (select id from profiles where role = 'admin' order by created_at limit 1);
  u jsonb; s jsonb; a jsonb;
  v_prob problems%rowtype; v_cur problem_versions%rowtype; v_have jsonb; v_want jsonb; v_new uuid;
  v_src mock_exam_sets%rowtype; v_new_set uuid; v_cols text; v_cols_i text; v_pids uuid[];
  v_n int; v_stale int; v_bad text; v_done_p int := 0; v_skip_p int := 0; v_done_s int := 0; v_skip_s int := 0;
begin
  if v_actor is null then raise exception 'No admin profile found.'; end if;

  -- Phase 1: problems -> new published problem version each (same flow as the admin problem editor)
  for u in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_plan->'problems') loop
    select * into v_prob from problems where id = (u->>'problem_id')::uuid;
    if v_prob.id is null then raise exception '[%] problem % not found', u->>'patch_id', u->>'problem_id'; end if;
    select * into v_cur from problem_versions where id = v_prob.published_version_id;
    if v_cur.id is null then raise exception '[%] problem % has no published version', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id; end if;
    -- final field values = current published version, overridden by the planned new values
    a := jsonb_build_object('passage', v_cur.passage, 'question', v_cur.question, 'options', v_cur.options, 'correct_index', v_cur.correct_index, 'answers', v_cur.answers,
                            'explanation', v_cur.explanation, 'explanation_en', v_cur.explanation_en, 'figure', v_cur.figure, 'statements', v_cur.statements, 'difficulty', v_cur.difficulty,
                            'figure_checked', coalesce(v_cur.figure_checked, false), 'evidence_target', v_cur.evidence_target, 'evidence_span', v_cur.evidence_span,
                            'answer_rationale', v_cur.answer_rationale, 'distractor_error_types', v_cur.distractor_error_types);
    v_have := (select coalesce(jsonb_object_agg(k, a->k), '{}'::jsonb) from jsonb_object_keys(u->'expect') k);
    v_want := (select coalesce(jsonb_object_agg(k, (a || (u->'set'))->k), '{}'::jsonb) from jsonb_object_keys(u->'expect') k);
    if v_have = v_want then v_skip_p := v_skip_p + 1; raise notice '[%] already applied, skipped', u->>'patch_id'; continue; end if;
    if v_have <> u->'expect' then raise exception '[%] DRIFT: the published version of problem % no longer matches the expected old content (re-run the dry-run)', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id; end if;
    a := a || (u->'set');
    if exists (select 1 from problem_versions where problem_id = v_prob.id and status in ('draft', 'in_review')) then
      raise exception '[%] problem % has an open draft/in_review version', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id;
    end if;
    v_new := public.save_problem_draft_version(
      p_problem_id => v_prob.id, p_passage => a->>'passage', p_options => nullif(a->'options', 'null'::jsonb), p_correct_index => (a->>'correct_index')::int,
      p_explanation => a->>'explanation', p_difficulty => a->>'difficulty', p_actor_id => v_actor, p_answers => nullif(a->'answers', 'null'::jsonb),
      p_figure => nullif(a->'figure', 'null'::jsonb), p_figure_checked => coalesce((a->>'figure_checked')::boolean, false), p_statements => nullif(a->'statements', 'null'::jsonb),
      p_question => a->>'question', p_repair_status => null, p_explanation_en => a->>'explanation_en', p_evidence_target => a->>'evidence_target',
      p_evidence_span => a->>'evidence_span', p_answer_rationale => a->>'answer_rationale', p_distractor_error_types => nullif(a->'distractor_error_types', 'null'::jsonb));
    perform public.set_problem_render_check(v_new, u->'render_check');
    perform public.set_problem_quality(v_new, coalesce(v_cur.quality, '{}'::jsonb) || jsonb_build_object('auditFix', u->'audit_fix'));
    perform public.confirm_and_publish_problem_version(v_new, v_actor);
    if u ? 'ap' then perform public.ap_attach_new_version(u->'ap'->>'candidate_key', (u->'ap'->>'item_index')::int, v_new, v_actor); end if;
    v_done_p := v_done_p + 1;
    raise notice '[%] problem % -> new version %', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id, v_new;
  end loop;

  -- Phase 2: sets -> new set version per affected published set (items of the patched problems point to the new problem versions; snapshots of the rest are copied)
  for s in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_plan->'sets') loop
    select array_agg(x::uuid) into v_pids from jsonb_array_elements_text(s->'problem_ids') x;
    select * into v_src from mock_exam_sets where set_group_id = (s->>'set_group_id')::uuid and status = 'published' and archived_at is null order by version_no desc limit 1 for update;
    if v_src.id is null then raise exception 'Set group % has no published version (%).', s->>'set_group_id', s->>'name'; end if;
    select count(*) into v_n from mock_exam_set_items i where i.exam_set_id = v_src.id and i.problem_id = any (v_pids);
    if v_n <> cardinality(v_pids) then raise exception 'Set % v% holds % of % target problems.', v_src.name, v_src.version_no, v_n, cardinality(v_pids); end if;
    select count(*) into v_stale from mock_exam_set_items i join problems p on p.id = i.problem_id
     where i.exam_set_id = v_src.id and i.problem_id = any (v_pids) and p.published_version_id is distinct from i.problem_version_id;
    if v_stale = 0 then v_skip_s := v_skip_s + 1; raise notice 'set % v% already up to date, skipped', v_src.name, v_src.version_no; continue; end if;
    perform pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtextextended('mock_exam_new_version:' || v_src.set_group_id::text, 0));
    if exists (select 1 from mock_exam_sets where set_group_id = v_src.set_group_id and status = 'draft') then
      raise exception 'A draft version already exists for set % - publish or archive it first.', v_src.name;
    end if;
    v_new_set := gen_random_uuid();
    select string_agg(quote_ident(column_name), ', ' order by ordinal_position) into v_cols
      from information_schema.columns where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'mock_exam_sets' and is_generated = 'NEVER'
       and column_name not in ('id', 'version_no', 'status', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'published_at', 'published_by', 'archived_at', 'access_tier');
    execute format('insert into mock_exam_sets (id, version_no, status, created_by, access_tier, %s) select $1, $2, ''draft'', $3, ''tutoring'', %s from mock_exam_sets where id = $4', v_cols, v_cols)
      using v_new_set, (select max(version_no) + 1 from mock_exam_sets where set_group_id = v_src.set_group_id), v_actor, v_src.id;
    select string_agg(quote_ident(column_name), ', ' order by ordinal_position),
           string_agg(case column_name
                        when 'problem_version_id' then 'case when i.problem_id = any ($3) then coalesce(p.published_version_id, i.problem_version_id) else i.problem_version_id end'
                        when 'content_snapshot' then 'case when i.problem_id = any ($3) then null else i.content_snapshot end'
                        else 'i.' || quote_ident(column_name) end, ', ' order by ordinal_position)
      into v_cols, v_cols_i
      from information_schema.columns where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'mock_exam_set_items' and is_generated = 'NEVER' and column_name not in ('id', 'exam_set_id', 'created_at');
    execute format('insert into mock_exam_set_items (exam_set_id, %s) select $1, %s from mock_exam_set_items i join problems p on p.id = i.problem_id where i.exam_set_id = $2', v_cols, v_cols_i)
      using v_new_set, v_src.id, v_pids;
    if v_src.format = 'mst' and not coalesce((public.mock_exam_validate_mst_set(v_new_set)->>'ready')::boolean, false) then
      raise exception 'New version of % is not ready (4-module blueprint check failed).', v_src.name;
    end if;
    select string_agg(x.problem_id::text || ':' || x.issue, ', ') into v_bad from (select * from public.mock_exam_set_item_issues(v_new_set) where issue is not null limit 5) x;
    if v_bad is not null then raise exception 'New version of % has item issues: %', v_src.name, v_bad; end if;
    perform public.mock_exam_publish_set(v_new_set, v_actor);
    v_done_s := v_done_s + 1;
    raise notice 'set % v% -> v% (%)', v_src.name, v_src.version_no, v_src.version_no + 1, v_new_set;
  end loop;
  raise notice 'DONE problems applied=% skipped=%; sets applied=% skipped=%', v_done_p, v_skip_p, v_done_s, v_skip_s;
end
$audit$;
